WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.933
- So not surprisingly,

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:03.410
everyone wants to know if
Roe versus Wade is dead.

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.810
And if the prior decision
of the Supreme Court

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.060
is any indication, the
answer is probably yes.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:09.893
As you may know,

00:00:09.893 --> 00:00:11.820
under the current Supreme
Court jurisprudence,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.870
under Casey versus Planned Parenthood,

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.340
abortion rights are basically governed

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.790
by a viability standard.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.400
Basically, abortions are legal

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.950
if it is done before
viability of the fetus.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.910
That is a change from the
original Roe vs. Wade standard

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.820
that dealt with the trimester framework.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.420
But when the Supreme
Court let the Texas law

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.920
that basically said no
abortions before six weeks,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.510
and maybe not even then,
it basically signaled

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.770
that Roe vs. Wade and its progeny is over,

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.010
including Casey versus Planned Parenthood.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.960
This was on the court's shadow docket,

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.570
so it carries no precedential effect.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.790
But if there was a majority of
justices on the Supreme Court

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.450
who still believed in a
constitutional right to abortion,

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.060
they would have stayed the proceedings

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.370
and not let the Texas law go into effect.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:52.060
But they didn't, which signals
that when this comes up

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.330
on the merits docket,

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.940
they will basically overturn Roe vs. Wade.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.840
But this is definitely
going to come up next term,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.553
so we'll see them in court.

